Third-party data and assets
---------------------------
- Food data looked up online comes from Open Food Facts (https://world.openfoodfacts.org) and is
  available under the Open Database License (ODbL) 1.0; individual contents under the Database
  Contents License. Foods saved from Open Food Facts keep that attribution in the app.
- Built-in generic food values are derived from USDA FoodData Central (https://fdc.nal.usda.gov),
  which is in the public domain (CC0 1.0). The offline food database (public/data/usda-foods.json)
  is converted from its Foundation Foods, SR Legacy and FNDDS datasets by scripts/build-usda.mjs.
- Manrope typeface, Copyright 2019 The Manrope Project Authors, SIL Open Font License 1.1
  (full text in LICENSES/OFL-1.1.txt).
- Barcode decoding in the web version uses zxing-wasm and barcode-detector (MIT).
- License texts of the bundled JavaScript libraries are listed in public/third-party-licenses.txt,
  which ships with the app.
- All illustrations, icons and animations in this repository are original to Satiago.

Privacy note on Google ML Kit
-----------------------------
The Android app scans barcodes with Google ML Kit, on the device. ML Kit logs usage diagnostics
through Google's Data Transport library; the app's manifest removes the registration of its upload
backend (com.google.android.datatransport.cct.CctBackendFactory), so those diagnostics have nowhere
to go and the app sends no ML Kit diagnostics to Google.

